IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTION 4: DEFENCES, ETC., AVAILABLE TO PROMISOR.
--
-- What is encoded: s 4(1) (when subsections (2) to (5) apply), (2) (what arises from the contract), (3) (what an
-- express term makes available), (4) (what would have been available against the third party as a party),
-- (5) (an express term can take (2) and (4) away) and (6) (the third party sued).  Each subsection answers on its
-- own (ruling E1, option C); `s 4 taken together` gathers (2), (3) and (4)(a) by hand (option B, as guidance only).
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Following the ruling of 2026-11-05 on
-- defences, JUST FALSE for a provision's defence means "this section gives no defence on these facts", and never
-- "the promisor has no defence at all".  The four grants of s 4(2), (3), (4)(a) and (4)(b) answer alike when a limb is
-- unmet: JUST FALSE, "this subsection gives no defence on these facts".  They are grants of a defence to a class of
-- matter, the matter that falls outside one grant may fall inside another, and the difference between "any matter
-- that" (s 4(2), (4)) and "any matter if" (s 4(3)) is a difference of grammar, not of what the subsection does
-- (fork G17 of NOTES.md).

§ `Section 4(1) -- when subsections (2) to (5) apply`

-- src:181 | 4.—(1) Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the
-- src:182 | enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in
-- src:183 | reliance on section 2.
@ref s 4(1) (src:181-183)
GIVEN `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` MEANS
    IF `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2."
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 4(5) -- an express term of the contract`

-- src:220 | (5) Subsections (2) and (4) are subject to any express term of the
-- src:221 | contract as to the matters that are not to be available to the promisor
-- src:222 | by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim.
@ref s 4(5) (src:220-222)
GIVEN `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` MEANS
    IF `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim`
    -- TRUE: the text's own "subject to any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subject-to reaches only "any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available"; with no such term it does not speak
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 4(2) to (4) -- what is available to the promisor`

-- (2): "any matter that (a) arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term; and (b) would
-- have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee."
-- src:185 | (2) The promisor has available to the promisor, by way of defence
-- src:186 | or set-off, any matter that —
-- src:188 | (a) arises from or in connection with the contract and is
-- src:189 | relevant to the term; and
-- src:191 | (b) would have been available to the promisor by way of
-- src:192 | defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by
-- src:193 | the promisee.
@ref s 4(2) (src:185-193)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (5) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", via s 4(1)): "Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2."
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the proceedings are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2 has not been stated
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a grant of a defence whose limb is unmet, worded as the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences words it: "this subsection gives no defence on these facts"; marginal reading M8): "any matter that (a) arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term; and (b) would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee"
        IF NOT (`the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` AND `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind ("subject to" read as the text's no; marginal reading M3): "Subsections (2) and (4) are subject to any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim."
        IF `s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:195 | (3) The promisor also has available to the promisor, by way of
-- src:196 | defence or set-off, any matter if —
-- src:198 | (a) an express term of the contract provides for it to be
-- src:199 | available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the
-- src:200 | third party; and
-- src:202 | (b) it would have been available to the promisor by way of
-- src:203 | defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by
-- src:204 | the promisee.
@ref s 4(3) (src:195-204)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (5) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", via s 4(1)): "Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2."
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the proceedings are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2 has not been stated
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the third party` AND `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "The promisor also has available to the promisor, by way of defence or set-off, any matter if — (a) an express term of the contract provides for it ...; and (b) it would have been available ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:209 | (4) The promisor also has available to the promisor —
-- src:211 | (a) by way of defence or set-off any matter; and
-- src:213 | (b) by way of counterclaim any matter not arising from the
-- src:214 | contract,
-- src:216 | that would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or
-- src:217 | set-off or by way of counterclaim against the third party (as the case
-- src:218 | may be) if the third party had been a party to the contract.
@ref s 4(4)(a) (src:209-211) (src:216-218)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (5) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", via s 4(1)): "Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2."
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the proceedings are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2 has not been stated
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a grant of a defence whose limb is unmet, "this subsection gives no defence on these facts"; marginal reading M8): "(a) by way of defence or set-off any matter ... that would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off ... against the third party ... if the third party had been a party to the contract"
        IF NOT `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind ("subject to" read as the text's no; marginal reading M3): "Subsections (2) and (4) are subject to any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim."
        IF `s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:209 | (4) The promisor also has available to the promisor —
-- src:213 | (b) by way of counterclaim any matter not arising from the
-- src:214 | contract,
-- src:216 | that would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or
-- src:217 | set-off or by way of counterclaim against the third party (as the case
-- src:218 | may be) if the third party had been a party to the contract.
@ref s 4(4)(b) (src:213-218)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (5) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the matter does not arise from the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of counterclaim against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", via s 4(1)): "Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2."
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the proceedings are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2 has not been stated
        IF `subsections (2) to (5) apply` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a grant of a defence whose limb is unmet, "this subsection gives no defence on these facts"; marginal reading M8): "(b) by way of counterclaim any matter not arising from the contract, that would have been available to the promisor by way of ... counterclaim against the third party ... if the third party had been a party to the contract"
        IF NOT (`the matter does not arise from the contract` AND `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of counterclaim against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind ("subject to" read as the text's no; marginal reading M3): "Subsections (2) and (4) are subject to any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim."
        IF `s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together -- gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B as guidance only)`

-- A matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if (2), (3) or (4)(a) makes it so.  JUST FALSE
-- here is "none of these three gives the matter on these facts" and is not "the promisor has no defence at all".
-- src:181 | 4.—(1) Subsections (2) to (5) apply where proceedings for the
-- src:182 | enforcement of a term of a contract are brought by a third party in
-- src:183 | reliance on section 2.
-- src:185 | (2) The promisor has available to the promisor, by way of defence
-- src:186 | or set-off, any matter that —
-- src:188 | (a) arises from or in connection with the contract and is
-- src:189 | relevant to the term; and
-- src:191 | (b) would have been available to the promisor by way of
-- src:192 | defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by
-- src:193 | the promisee.
-- src:195 | (3) The promisor also has available to the promisor, by way of
-- src:196 | defence or set-off, any matter if —
-- src:198 | (a) an express term of the contract provides for it to be
-- src:199 | available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the
-- src:200 | third party; and
-- src:202 | (b) it would have been available to the promisor by way of
-- src:203 | defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by
-- src:204 | the promisee.
-- src:209 | (4) The promisor also has available to the promisor —
-- src:211 | (a) by way of defence or set-off any matter; and
-- src:213 | (b) by way of counterclaim any matter not arising from the
-- src:214 | contract,
-- src:216 | that would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or
-- src:217 | set-off or by way of counterclaim against the third party (as the case
-- src:218 | may be) if the third party had been a party to the contract.
@ref s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together (src:181-218)
GIVEN `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` MEANS
    `three-valued OR`
        (`s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (`s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2`) `the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim`)
        (`three-valued OR`
            (`s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` (`s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2`) `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings brought by the third party` `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the proceedings had been brought by the promisee`)
            (`s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (`s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` `proceedings for the enforcement of a term of the contract are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2`) `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against the third party if the third party had been a party to the contract` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim`))

§ `Section 4(6) -- the third party sued`

-- src:224 | (6) Where, in any proceedings brought against a third party, the
-- src:225 | third party seeks to enforce a term of a contract (including, in
-- src:226 | particular, a term purporting to exclude or limit liability) in reliance
-- src:227 | on section 2, the third party may not do so if the third party could not
-- src:228 | have done so (whether by reason of any particular circumstances
-- src:229 | relating to the third party or otherwise) had the third party been a
-- src:230 | party to the contract.
@ref s 4(6) (src:224-230)
GIVEN `proceedings are brought against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party seeks to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party could not have done so had the third party been a party to the contract` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Where, in any proceedings brought against a third party, the third party seeks to enforce a term of a contract (including, in particular, a term purporting to exclude or limit liability) in reliance on section 2"
        IF NOT (`proceedings are brought against the third party` AND `the third party seeks to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- TRUE: the text's own "may not ... if"
        IF `the third party could not have done so had the third party been a party to the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "the third party may not do so if the third party could not have done so (whether by reason of any particular circumstances relating to the third party or otherwise) had the third party been a party to the contract"
        IF `the third party could not have done so had the third party been a party to the contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the third party could have done so as a party is a counterfactual the person has not stated
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `The regulative rule derived from s 4(6) (no time limit is stated, so none is given)`

-- The text names the bearer of the prohibition: "the third party may not do so".
-- src:224 | (6) Where, in any proceedings brought against a third party, the
-- src:225 | third party seeks to enforce a term of a contract (including, in
-- src:226 | particular, a term purporting to exclude or limit liability) in reliance
-- src:227 | on section 2, the third party may not do so if the third party could not
-- src:228 | have done so (whether by reason of any particular circumstances
-- src:229 | relating to the third party or otherwise) had the third party been a
-- src:230 | party to the contract.
@ref s 4(6) the prohibition (src:224-230)
GIVEN `proceedings are brought against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party seeks to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party could not have done so had the third party been a party to the contract` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 4(6) the third party SHANT enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` MEANS
    IF `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` `proceedings are brought against the third party` `the third party seeks to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` `the third party could not have done so had the third party been a party to the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the third party` SHANT `enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party`
    ELSE FULFILLED
